  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "The sole completed experiment (config_001: rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) yielded a very low validation accuracy of 48.5%, establishing a weak RNA-only baseline. With 8 experiments remaining, the most critical unknown is whether the image modality carries stronger signal than RNA for this task. config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) is a clean, single-variable comparison against config_001: it changes only the modality while keeping the profile setting (singleprofile) and architectural simplicity (no aggregation/fusion) identical. If image accuracy substantially exceeds 48.5%, the remaining budget should pivot toward image-centric or multimodal configurations; if it is comparable or lower, RNA improvements (better encoders, multiprofile) or multimodal fusion become the priority. This modality-level comparison is the highest-information experiment to guide the rest of the search and avoids committing to a specific encoder or fusion strategy before knowing which modality is most informative."
}

